1
00:04:42,352 --> 00:04:48,352
Hungry for Adventure...Burning to Fight!

2
00:09:24,705 --> 00:09:30,705
Johnny Tremain is a drama, family, war film directed by Robert Stevenson.

3
00:14:07,058 --> 00:14:13,058
When an injury bars him from pursuing his trade, Revolutionary War-era silversmith's apprentice Johnny Tremain finds a new life
in the ranks of the Sons of Liberty army, taking part in the Boston Tea Party and Paul Revere's legendary ride.

4
00:18:49,411 --> 00:18:55,411
Johnny Tremain, played by Hal Stalmaster.

5
00:23:31,764 --> 00:23:37,764
Rab Silsbee, played by Richard Beymer.

6
00:28:14,117 --> 00:28:20,117
Cilla Lapham, played by Luana Patten.

7
00:32:56,470 --> 00:33:02,470
James Otis, played by Jeff York.

8
00:37:38,823 --> 00:37:44,823
Jonathan Lyte, played by Sebastian Cabot.

9
00:42:21,176 --> 00:42:27,176
Samuel Adams, played by Rusty Lane.

10
00:47:03,529 --> 00:47:09,529
Johnny Tremain is a work of historical fiction written in 1943 by Esther Forbes that is
set in Boston prior to and during the outbreak of the American Revolution.

11
00:51:45,882 --> 00:51:51,882
Intended for teen-aged readers, the novel's themes include apprenticeship, courtship, sacrifice,
human rights, and the growing tension between Patriots and Loyalists as conflict nears.

12
00:56:28,235 --> 00:56:34,235
Events depicted in the novel include the Boston Tea Party, the British blockade of the Port of
Boston, the midnight ride of Paul Revere, and the Battles of Lexington and Concord.

13
01:01:10,588 --> 01:01:16,588
The book won the 1944 Newbery Medal and was believed to be "among the 20 best-selling children's books of the 20th century." It was estimated
to be the 16th-bestselling children's paperback book as of the year 2001 in the United States, according to Publishers Weekly.

14
01:05:52,941 --> 01:05:58,941
In 1957, Walt Disney Pictures released a film
adaptation, also called Johnny Tremain.

15
01:10:35,294 --> 01:10:41,294
The film explores themes of patriot, merchant, sons of liberity.

16
01:15:17,647 --> 01:15:23,647
The tone is emotional.
